    "final_text": "Fixed: `buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false`. I confirmed the bug first: the repro URL came out as `https://api.example.test/webhooks/deliveries?dry_run=true`.\n\n**Root cause:** In `src/url-builder.js`, `serializeQuery` (line 126) skipped any value that wasn't truthy (`if (!value) continue;`). That drops `0`, `false` and `''`, not just missing values. `appendQueryValue` (line 137) had the same check for array items, so `{ attempt: [0, 1] }` also lost its `0`. The issue doesn't mention this, but it's the same bug.\n\n**Fix (2 lines):** Both checks now skip only `undefined` and `null`. That's the same rule `normalizePath` already uses for path segments in this file. The builder's API is unchanged.\n\n**Regression tests** in `tests/url-builder.test.js`:\n- `buildUrl keeps zero and false query values (ISSUE-214)`: the exact repro from the issue, checked against the full expected URL.\n- `serializeQuery keeps falsy array items but skips null and undefined`: `0` and `false` inside arrays are kept, and `null`/`undefined` are still left out.\n\nI ran the suite with the fix removed: both new tests failed and the other 7 passed. With the fix, `npm test` passes 9/9.\n\n**Behavior change:** An empty-string value (`{ q: '' }`) is now sent as `q=` instead of being dropped. I think that's right, since the issue asks for values to be included exactly, and callers can still leave a key out by passing `null` or `undefined`. It could still affect anyone who used `''` to mean \"leave this out\", so I noted it in the `ISSUE.md` Resolution section along with the fixed code path and the tests.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
